  "limitations": [
    "No live Pico network reception: body/trigger readers use a 90Hz replay SDK shim. Native RPC/packet parsing overhead is absent.",
    "Current real right-wrist feedback has TIMEOUT. Policy inputs use the recorded feedback, so this cannot validate live feedback health or EXTERNAL motion.",
    "No control publisher, wire publication, firmware ingress/ack, or closed-loop physical response.",
    "Three repeats per challenger with fixed order ABAB reduce order/temperature uncertainty but are not a randomized long-duration acceptance.",
    "Native objective code is an isolated prototype, not part of the sealed production delivery. Full integration/version guards and live validation remain."
  ],
  "recommendation": "For the next live read-only trial, spawn input before pinning control to CPU2-4; retain GMR CPU1. Test the native2 prototype only after integration/guard checks. Do not claim stable <10ms/<20ms acceptance.",
